## cr-03 gate-fix session: merge with manus-parity (O6 tip 603d71c), all gates green

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity: run git merge
manus-parity, resolve all conflicts keeping both sides, commit.`

### The failure that was fixed
`git merge manus-parity` (parity tip `603d71c`, the O6 merge that added `eventLogMigrate`
and `inputQueue`) conflicted in exactly ONE file: the tracked rollup marker `.jdone`
(add/add). No source file conflicted and no source file needed editing. Every other file
auto-merged cleanly with the `ort` strategy.

### Root cause
Both branches prepend a new report section at the same top-of-file anchor in the tracked
rollup marker `.jdone`, so Git cannot pick a side and emits an add/add conflict. The
conflict is bookkeeping-only; it is not a code divergence.

### What was done
- Extracted both sides with `git show :2:.jdone` (ours) and `git show :3:.jdone` (theirs).
- Resolved the 4 conflict hunks by keeping BOTH sides, with CRLF normalized before matching
  (`/^<<<<<<< /`, `/^=======$/`, `/^>>>>>>> /`).
- Verified mechanically: 0 line-start conflict markers; the resolved `.jdone` is a
  wrap-tolerant superset of both sides (the only "missing" lines were re-wrapped duplicates
  of already-present sentences); both report headings are present.
- Committed the merge as `a57f255` (parity tip `603d71c`). No source file was modified.

### Gate condition verified
- `git merge manus-parity` -> `Already up to date.`
- `git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD` -> exit 0
- `git rev-list --left-right --count manus-parity...HEAD` -> `0  8`
- `git status --porcelain` -> empty (clean tree)
- `.jdone` committed at 2713 lines; both sides' report sections intact; 0 conflict markers

### Gates (all run from the worktree root on the committed tree `a57f255`)
- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server` -> exit 0 (`dist\server.cjs 19.4mb`, pdf worker copied)
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)` -> exit 0 (Next.js 16.4.2, Turbopack)
- `npm run check:encoding` -> OK (no BOM, no mojibake, all JSON valid)
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run src/components/workspace)` -> 8 files, 74 tests passed
- `node --import tsx --test` (codingPrompt, ciWatch, verifyAndRecord, prVerification, eventLog, prReview) -> 99 tests passed, 0 failed
- `.jdone` integrity: U+FFFD 0, `???` 0, Arabic codepoints 208, no BOM

### Files
- `.jdone` (merge resolution only; both sides kept)

