skipped, and no code was dropped:

1. `src/agent/masterPromptText.ts` was stored as a BINARY file whose working-tree
   bytes were 52569 bytes of all-NUL (corrupted) on BOTH our side and the
   merge-base; manus-parity carried the real 58896-byte asset. It was regenerated
   with `npm run gen:master-prompt`, which produced a file byte-identical to
   manus-parity's (blob 145cc3a0), so the parity asset was kept.
2. `src/agent/loop.ts`: resolution keeps the repo-local skill precedence
   (`loadProjectSkills(opts.cfg.workspace).skills`) AND parity's `opts.prompt`
   argument, plus `opts.sandboxMode`.
3. `src/server/routes/craft.ts`: the duplicated `CraftRouteOptions` block was
   removed; both the `CraftRouteOptions` interface and the `root` resolution from
   manus-parity are kept.
4. `src/agent/__tests__/__snapshots__/coding-prompt.snap.json`: the master-prompt
   hash was recomputed from the merged state (via a throwaway generator that was
   deleted afterwards) and matches manus-parity's committed hash.

The merge also exposed one real type error: parity's
`src/agent/__tests__/cacheUsageAccounting.test.ts` test factory omitted the
`skills` config field that D10 added to `Config`. It was fixed by adding
`skills: { autoSuggest: false, suggestModel: "" }` to the factory (commit 54cfc81).

