## O6 complete: durable input queue + agent-loop admit hook

`src/server/inputQueue.ts` (132 lines, from BUILD_SPEC §6.6) with `enqueue` /
`admitPending` / `markAdmitted` / `cancel` / `drop` / `admitAllPending`, plus the loop
wiring that admits a queued message at an agent step boundary via
`append('input', ..., { idempotencyKey: q.id })` + `markAdmitted`.

Acceptance (plan row O6: "message sent during a busy run survives restart and is
admitted once") is covered by passing automated tests:
- `src/server/__tests__/inputQueue.test.ts` (12 tests): stores as received without
  appending a log event, session isolation, admits pending once in arrival order,
  idempotent across a crash between append and markAdmitted, survives a restart,
  no re-admit after a restart, markAdmitted records the sequence and ignores unknown
  ids, cancel/drop semantics, boot sweep, arrival order on tied timestamps, steering
  distinct from queued delivery.
- `src/server/__tests__/inputQueueAdmit.test.ts` (3 tests): the loop admit hook admits a
  message that arrives mid-run exactly once at a step boundary, admits nothing when no
  hook is wired, and never fails the run when the hook throws.

Test commands:
  node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/inputQueue.test.ts src/server/__tests__/inputQueueAdmit.test.ts

