V11 complete: design_critique — vision rubric critique loop for generated UIs.

## Preserved: manus-parity .jdone (V11 design_critique report)

What shipped
------------
A new always-on agent tool, `design_critique`, that scores a built interface against
the Loam UI Kit rubric by sending the captured screenshots to the vision model. It
reuses the existing `visualReview` (Ollama vision) and the `preview_screenshot`
capture machinery rather than duplicating either.

- `src/design/critique.ts` (extended, +489):
  - `CRITIQUE_DIMENSION_IDS` = hierarchy, spacing, contrast, alignment,
    color-count, overflow, rtl. Blocking dimensions: contrast, overflow, rtl.
    Per-dimension floor 60, pass threshold 80 on the mean, max 2 fix rounds,
    max 2 model repair attempts.
  - `normalizeCritiqueVerdict`: strict rubric contract. Every dimension exactly
    once, numeric score, non-empty note. `accept` requires an empty issues list,
    every dimension at or above the floor, and the mean at or above the
    threshold; `revise` must name at least one visible defect; the `rtl` dimension
    must be exactly 100 on an `ltr` page. The mean is always recomputed from the
    dimensions and the declared `score` is ignored, so a model cannot inflate its
    own verdict.
  - `critiquePasses`: gates on the blocking dimensions independently of the mean.
  - `runVisionCritique`: throws `VisualReviewUnavailable` when no client or no
    readable screenshot, retries a malformed answer with the validation errors,
    reads screenshots from disk as base64 images, reports `source: "model"`.
  - `runCritiqueLoop`: rounds 0..maxRounds, `instruction = fixes[0] ?? issues[0] ?? ""`,
    accumulates usage across rounds, always reports the best score it saw.
- `src/tools/designCritique.ts` (new): `createDesignCritiqueTools(preview, { ollama })`,
  `formatCritiqueReport` (reports round/maxRounds), `lintSiteDirectory`,
  `captureForCritique`, and a deterministic `fallbackCritique` for the no-model path.
  Params: `dir`, `url`, `screenshots`, `source`, `prompt`, `language`, `direction`,
  `brief`, `threshold`, `maxAttempts`, `round`, `maxRounds`, `format`.
  One critique call per invocation; the caller drives the edit/rebuild/capture loop.
  At the last allowed round the report says the round budget is exhausted and tells
  the caller to stop; otherwise it says to apply the first fix, rebuild, capture
  again and call with `round=N+1`. Returns `{ ok: verdict === "accept" }`.
- `src/design/tokenLint.ts`: `lintSiteSource()` lints one in-memory source with the
  same rules as the filesystem linter (so an editor buffer and a directory on disk
  are scored by one code path); `SiteRule` exported; `runCritiqueLoop`'s `options`
  argument is now required.
- Wiring: registered in `src/index.ts` and added to `ALWAYS_ON_TOOLS` in
  `src/server/runTools.ts`; the build Implement phase now instructs
  lint -> capture -> critique with `design_lint`, `preview_screenshot`,
  `design_critique`; `DESIGN_CRITIQUE_PROMPT` in `src/modes/designRules.ts` is
  pushed into the system prompt when the tool is present (`src/agent/prompt.ts`).

All prompts, tool descriptions and rules are original Loam wording.

Acceptance test (V11 spec)
--------------------------
"A mock vision model drives a fix round; the threshold logic is tested" — covered by
`src/design/__tests__/critique.test.ts` (31 tests) and
`src/tools/__tests__/designCritique.test.ts` (11 tests):
- fake and sequence Ollama clients, no network, no real model;
- `revise` -> `accept` drives exactly one fix round, with the second call receiving
  the first round's fix instruction;
- round budget exhaustion, custom threshold, floor/mean threshold logic;
- safety gates: a high mean with a failing contrast/overflow/rtl still fails;
- `rtl` must be exactly 100 on an `ltr` page, and an Arabic RTL page is gated on it;
- an unusable model answer never becomes a pass;
- deterministic fallback, JSON output, always-on + prompt wiring.

